getaddrinfo with no name and no AI_PASSIVE gave the IPv4 loopback
address in the machine's byte order: 1.0.0.127 on x86-64, where binding
or connecting fails with EADDRNOTAVAIL. ssh -L and -D without a bind
address listened on ::1 alone, so a client of 127.0.0.1 was refused.
The address is now in network order, as every in_addr_t is.
Meant for upstream.

--- a/options/posix/generic/lookup.cpp
+++ b/options/posix/generic/lookup.cpp
@@ -959,7 +959,9 @@
 			struct dns_addr_buf addr_buf;
 			addr_buf.family = AF_INET;
 
-			in_addr_t addr = INADDR_LOOPBACK;
+			// In network order, as every in_addr_t: on a little-endian
+			// machine INADDR_LOOPBACK itself is 1.0.0.127.
+			in_addr_t addr = htonl(INADDR_LOOPBACK);
 			memcpy(&addr_buf.addr, &addr, 4);
 
 			buf.buf.push_back(addr_buf);
